WEBVTT

00:00:10.478 --> 00:00:11.259
George C.

00:00:11.319 --> 00:00:17.962
Stars by Dave Cooper.

00:00:18.022 --> 00:00:28.498
The Happy Holiday Hotel is a small English hotel near the sea.

00:00:28.559 --> 00:00:31.700
These people work there.

00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.753
George, the hotel manager.

00:00:35.813 --> 00:00:42.782
Mary, she helps George George and Mary are married.

00:00:42.842 --> 00:00:46.204
Judy, the cook.

00:00:46.264 --> 00:00:49.526
Peter, an old man.

00:00:49.586 --> 00:01:02.642
He helps outside in the garden and carries the bags in the hotel.

00:01:02.702 --> 00:01:14.596
Scene 1, the telephone call.

00:01:14.656 --> 00:01:19.679
In the Happy Holiday Hotel, it is 3 o'clock.

00:01:19.739 --> 00:01:22.791
George is talking to Mary.

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:27.684
The telephone rings.

00:01:27.744 --> 00:01:31.836
Hello?

00:01:31.896 --> 00:01:34.087
Happy Holiday Hotel?

00:01:34.147 --> 00:01:36.608
George Harris here?

00:01:36.668 --> 00:01:40.237
Yes, I am the manager.

00:01:40.297 --> 00:01:42.755
Tony who?

00:01:42.815 --> 00:01:47.258
Oh, Tony Maddock the TV star.

00:01:47.318 --> 00:01:50.650
Your Tony Maddock's secretary.

00:01:50.709 --> 00:01:52.511
I see.

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:55.452
Yes, that's fine.

00:01:55.512 --> 00:02:01.235
You want a large room for Tony and he wants to see the sea.

00:02:01.295 --> 00:02:02.556
Right?

00:02:02.616 --> 00:02:04.927
Yes, yes.

00:02:04.987 --> 00:02:06.178
I know.

00:02:06.238 --> 00:02:08.519
Tony is very important.

00:02:08.579 --> 00:02:11.004
A TV star.

00:02:11.064 --> 00:02:12.910
Yes.

00:02:12.969 --> 00:02:15.110
Fish, you say?

00:02:15.170 --> 00:02:18.161
Yes, that's easy.

00:02:18.221 --> 00:02:20.152
Right then.

00:02:20.212 --> 00:02:25.413
Today, Tony's coming today.

00:02:25.473 --> 00:02:27.123
Fine.

00:02:27.183 --> 00:02:30.835
Goodbye, and thank you.

00:02:30.894 --> 00:02:35.196
George puts down the telephone.

00:02:35.255 --> 00:02:37.382
Today!

00:02:37.442 --> 00:02:41.270
Tony's coming today, Mary.

00:02:41.330 --> 00:02:44.632
Listen, I've got good news.

00:02:44.692 --> 00:02:47.334
Don't shout, George.

00:02:47.394 --> 00:02:48.645
What is it?

00:02:48.705 --> 00:02:50.456
Tony Mattock.

00:02:50.516 --> 00:02:58.552
You know, the television star is coming to our hotel this afternoon.

00:02:58.612 --> 00:03:02.916
Tony Mattock, he's famous.

00:03:02.975 --> 00:03:06.971
He's coming here at five o'clock today.

00:03:07.030 --> 00:03:10.664
He's a TV star, you say?

00:03:10.724 --> 00:03:13.204
Is he in Neighbours?

00:03:13.264 --> 00:03:15.855
I don't watch TV very much.

00:03:15.915 --> 00:03:17.556
Neighbours?

00:03:17.616 --> 00:03:18.906
Probably.

00:03:18.926 --> 00:03:24.417
He's going to have our best room and our best food.

00:03:24.477 --> 00:03:27.408
I'm going to look at the room now.

00:03:27.468 --> 00:03:30.929
Fine, George, but I'm busy.

00:03:30.989 --> 00:03:32.999
I'm going to the supermarket.

00:03:33.059 --> 00:03:35.386
Don't be silly, Mary.

00:03:35.446 --> 00:03:38.324
You can't go to the shops now.

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:40.224
He is a famous man.

00:03:40.244 --> 00:03:45.886
Do you understand an important person?

00:03:45.946 --> 00:03:48.117
Tony Marduk.

00:03:48.177 --> 00:03:50.148
I don't know him.

00:03:50.207 --> 00:03:52.318
Is he very rich?

00:03:52.378 --> 00:03:54.379
I don't know, Mary.

00:03:54.439 --> 00:03:56.359
But he's very important.

00:03:56.419 --> 00:03:57.830
I know that.

00:03:57.890 --> 00:03:59.030
Yes.

00:03:59.090 --> 00:04:02.268
Well, I'm going to the shops now.

00:04:02.328 --> 00:04:04.245
See you later, George.

00:04:04.305 --> 00:04:04.806
Good.

00:04:04.866 --> 00:04:06.036
Merry.

00:04:06.096 --> 00:04:12.070
Stop.

00:04:12.130 --> 00:04:18.226
Scene two.

00:04:18.286 --> 00:04:21.648
Fish for dinner.

00:04:21.707 --> 00:04:27.012
In the kitchen.

00:04:27.071 --> 00:04:32.126
Good morning, Judy.

00:04:32.186 --> 00:04:34.480
We've got good news.

00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:37.282
Tony Maddock is coming today.

00:04:37.342 --> 00:04:39.484
The famous TV star.

00:04:39.544 --> 00:04:40.986
Tony Ho.

00:04:41.046 --> 00:04:43.237
I don't think I know the name.

00:04:43.297 --> 00:04:45.159
I don't like TV.

00:04:45.219 --> 00:04:46.810
I like reading.

00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.982
Tony Maddock.

00:04:49.042 --> 00:04:50.243
That's right.

00:04:50.303 --> 00:04:51.975
Tony Maddock.

00:04:52.034 --> 00:04:54.857
Now, what have you got for dinner?

00:04:54.917 --> 00:04:57.373
Have you got any fish?

00:04:57.433 --> 00:05:00.288
He likes fish, his secretary says.

00:05:00.348 --> 00:05:03.800
No, I haven't got any fish today, Mr. Harris.

00:05:03.860 --> 00:05:06.122
Sorry, I've got some chicken.

00:05:06.182 --> 00:05:09.273
No, he wants fish.

00:05:09.333 --> 00:05:11.164
Can you buy some?

00:05:11.224 --> 00:05:13.165
Oh, no, Mr. Harris.

00:05:13.225 --> 00:05:15.616
I never buy fish on Thursdays.

00:05:15.676 --> 00:05:17.688
I always buy chicken.

00:05:17.748 --> 00:05:22.840
Well, his secretary says fish, not chicken, right?

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.701
No, shout at me.

00:05:24.761 --> 00:05:26.338
I don't like it.

00:05:26.398 --> 00:05:27.446
I'm leaving.

00:05:27.466 --> 00:05:29.628
I'm not going to buy anything.

00:05:29.688 --> 00:05:31.158
I'm going home.

00:05:31.218 --> 00:05:35.832
No, Judy, please stop.

00:05:35.892 --> 00:05:37.944
I'm sorry, Judy.

00:05:38.004 --> 00:05:40.526
You're a good cook, Judy.

00:05:40.586 --> 00:05:42.438
A beautiful cook.

00:05:42.498 --> 00:05:45.160
Please don't leave now.

00:05:45.220 --> 00:05:49.814
Mr. Maddock is coming here today and he wants fish.

00:05:49.874 --> 00:05:57.201
Please, please, please, Judy, go and buy some nice fish.

00:05:57.260 --> 00:06:02.134
No, it's chicken on first days, right?

00:06:02.194 --> 00:06:05.366
Oh, okay, Judy.

00:06:05.426 --> 00:06:12.670
Chicken.

00:06:12.730 --> 00:06:19.844
